      "type": "textEditor",
      "data": {
        "value": "<p>TEST DETAILS<br>-----------------------------------------<br>Marker Tested : OLIG2 (Oligodendrocyte Transcription Factor 2)<br>Clone &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; : __________________________<br>Control &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; : Positive Control Used<br>Method &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;: Immunohistochemistry</p>\n<p>RESULTS<br>-----------------------------------------<br>Marker : OLIG2<br>Result : Positive / Negative / Focal<br>Staining Pattern : Nuclear staining in tumor cells<br>Proportion of Positive Cells : ______ %</p>\n<p>INTERPRETATION CRITERIA<br>-----------------------------------------<br>- OLIG2 Positive: Suggestive of glial origin, especially oligodendroglial or astrocytic tumors<br>- OLIG2 Negative: Does not support glial lineage; consider other differential diagnoses</p>\n<p>IMPRESSION<br>-----------------------------------------<br>[ ] OLIG2 Positive &ndash; Supports diagnosis of glioma (correlate with other glial markers)<br>[ ] OLIG2 Negative &ndash; Does not support glial differentiation<br>[ ] Correlate with histopathology, IDH1, GFAP, ATRX, Ki-67 for grading</p>\n<p>COMMENTS<br>-----------------------------------------<br>- OLIG2 is a nuclear transcription factor expressed in oligodendrogliomas and astrocytomas<br>- Used as part of the immunohistochemical panel for CNS tumors</p>",
        "field": "textEditor"
      },
